body:
Possible issues:

+ [`NgComponentOutlet`](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/5.2.9/packages/common/src/directives/ng_component_outlet.ts#L10-L112) and [`NgTemplateOutlet`](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/5.2.9/packages/common/src/directives/ng_template_outlet.ts#L10-L100) doesn't have `TemplateRef` but known as Structural Directive;
+ [`NgSwitch`](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/5.2.9/packages/common/src/directives/ng_switch.ts#L35-L127) and [`NgPlural`](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/5.2.9/packages/common/src/directives/ng_plural.ts#L14-L81) has no `TemplateRef` nor `ViewContainerRef`, only their content children companions do;
+ [`RouterOutlet `](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/5.2.9/packages/router/src/directives/router_outlet.ts#L14-L142) is technically more Structural Directive (providing `ViewContainerRef` like `NgComponentOutlet`) than Attribute Directive (doesn't perform side-effects at all), but using element selector making that weird.
